# Files that are exempt from the test-coverage check.
# One path per line, relative to the binate repo root.
# Example: pkg/builtins/rt/rt.bn

# === GENUINE EXCEPTIONS — internal helpers / per-platform ABI ========
# Files that legitimately have no per-file _test.bn, exercised instead by a
# package-level test (and conformance / e2e where noted).  The standard is a
# sibling _test.bn per non-test .bn; this list should hold only genuine
# exceptions (no "TEMPORARY, add a test later" entries — those get a test).
#
# Math internal helpers + constants + an operation-split type:
#   bessel01_asymp / trig_reduce are unexported helpers (no public surface to
#   test directly — covered through the public bessel/trig functions); const is
#   just constants; big/nat is a type exercised across nat_arith/div/shift_test.
impls/stdlib/pkg/std/math/bessel01_asymp.bn
impls/stdlib/pkg/std/math/big/nat.bn
impls/stdlib/pkg/std/math/const.bn
impls/stdlib/pkg/std/math/trig_reduce.bn
#
# rt_baremetal.bn is the bare-metal RefDec/panic-writer variant, build-gated
# (is(os, "baremetal")) so it's absent from the hosted unit-test build and
# can't carry a hosted per-file _test.bn (like args_baremetal.bn / sys_baremetal.bn).
impls/core/common/pkg/builtins/rt/rt_baremetal.bn
#
# rt_managed.bn is the target-agnostic managed/refcount layer (Alloc / Free / RefInc / RefDec /
# ZeroRefDestroy / Refcount / Box / MakeManagedSlice / headerPtr / MemCopy + the fault
# checks), split out of rt.bn / rt_baremetal.bn so it is defined once.  Its functions ARE the rt
# package's public managed surface, exercised directly by rt_test.bn (the package's test file) and
# by every managed-allocation conformance/unit test on every target — no separate per-file _test.bn.
impls/core/common/pkg/builtins/rt/rt_managed.bn
#
# rt_memzero.bn is the portable word-at-a-time rt.MemZero, the fallback for every arch except
# aarch64 (which links a hand-asm wide-store MemZero of the same symbol).  MemZero is exercised
# exhaustively by rt_test.bn (TestMemZeroAlignmentsAndSizes etc.) on every target — testing the
# portable body on non-aarch64 and the hand-asm on aarch64 — so it needs no per-file _test.bn
# (and one gated to !aarch64 would leave the aarch64 hand-asm untested).
impls/core/common/pkg/builtins/rt/rt_memzero.bn
#
# reflect.bn holds fallback TypeOf / DataOf bodies for the non-inlined path (the
# func taken as a value / VM-dispatched by name); a DIRECT call is a compiler
# intrinsic lowered inline.  A per-file _test.bn would have to reconstruct
# interface values exactly like the conformance test does, so the bodies are
# covered by conformance/1261_reflect_funcvalue (inlined vs func-value differential).
impls/core/common/pkg/builtins/reflect/reflect.bn
#
# startup entry glue: args_main.bn holds _entry, the compiled-only c_export'd
# `main` (native FFI — it __c_call's bn_entry), which is not unit-testable in
# isolation: it is the process entry, interpreting it hits the __c_call/native-only
# gate, and calling it re-enters bn_entry.  Its argv capture is exercised
# end-to-end by e2e/os-args.sh (argc/argv round-trip, compiled AND interpreted,
# now asserting argv[0] is populated) and its reachability by
# conformance/spec/17-program/011; the shared arg-shaping helpers live in args.bn
# (covered by args_test.bn).
impls/core/common/pkg/builtins/startup/args_main.bn
#
# args_baremetal.bn is the bare-metal counterpart of args_main.bn: a build-gated
# (is(entrypoint, "start")) startup __init side effect that installs the 1-element
# empty-placeholder argv on a bare-metal image (which has no argv-installing entry).
# It is EXCLUDED from a hosted build (entrypoint "main"), so it is absent from the
# unit-test build and cannot have a host per-file _test.bn; it is exercised
# end-to-end by conformance/stdlib/os/011_args on both baremetal lanes (which it
# turns green), and the shared arg-shaping helpers it calls (SetArgs) live in
# args.bn (covered by args_test.bn).
impls/core/common/pkg/builtins/startup/args_baremetal.bn
#
# common.EmitObject is the object-emission SKELETON that native backends
# delegate to; its per-arch steps are ArchEmitter method calls.  A standalone
# unit test would need a full 14-method mock ArchEmitter for marginal added
# value — it is exercised end-to-end by native conformance tests plus each
# backend's emit-shape unit tests (aarch64 routes through it now; x64/arm32 as
# they convert).  The per-arch impls (aarch64Emitter etc.) DO carry sibling
# _test.bn files.
pkg/binate/native/common/common_emit_object.bn
# regalloc_fuse_liveness.bn holds the element-GEP-fusion redirect hooks
# (fusedGepBaseIdx / isFusedGepDef / mark* used by the liveness + interval scans);
# exercised by the FusableElemGeps tests (common_elem_gep_fuse_test.bn), the
# liveness/interval tests, and the aa64 fused load/store conformance path.
pkg/binate/native/common/regalloc_fuse_liveness.bn
#
# testing/sys sys_host.bn / sys_baremetal.bn are the per-target WriteStdout sinks
# (host: write(2) on fd 1 via __c_call; bare metal: the semihosting console).  A
# __c_call / semihost stdout write is not unit-testable in isolation — the host
# harness can't capture fd 1 — and sys_baremetal.bn is build-gated (is(os,
# "baremetal")), so it is absent from the hosted unit-test build entirely (like
# rt_baremetal.bn / args_baremetal.bn above).  Both are exercised end-to-end by
# testing.Print/Println across every conformance mode; the package's TestResult type
# (its only other export) lives in sys.bni.
impls/core/common/pkg/builtins/testing/sys/sys_host.bn
impls/core/common/pkg/builtins/testing/sys/sys_baremetal.bn
#
# inline_eligibility.bn is the inliner's callee-shape gate (inlinableCallee +
# the isCallFamilyOp / isInlinableResultType classifiers), extracted from
# inline_calls.bn purely for file length.  It is a set of predicates with no
# standalone surface; it is exercised by inline_calls_test.bn (which drives
# inlinableCallee through inlineCalls) and the vm / codegen inliner tests.
pkg/binate/ir/inline_eligibility.bn
#
# defer IR-gen (§14.13) split across three files.  gen_defer.bn carries the
# per-file gen_defer_test.bn (structural invariants); the store/exit half
# (gen_defer_exit.bn) and the two coercion/decl helpers extracted purely to keep
# their origin files under the length limit are exercised by the same tests plus
# the defer conformance suite (conformance/12*_defer_*) across LLVM / VM / native:
pkg/binate/irgen/gen_defer_exit.bn
# gen_call_coerce.bn — coerceArg's eager/delivery phase split (extracted from
# gen_call.bn); covered by gen_call_test.bn + every call/defer conformance test.
pkg/binate/irgen/gen_call_coerce.bn
# gen_decl_stmt.bn — genDecl, moved out of gen_stmt.bn for length; covered by
# gen_stmt_test.bn + the var/const-decl conformance tests.
pkg/binate/irgen/gen_decl_stmt.bn
# gen_defer_build.bn — per-shape defer-site builders, split from gen_defer.bn
# for length; covered by gen_defer_test.bn + the defer conformance suite.
pkg/binate/irgen/gen_defer_build.bn

# The irgen extraction relocated shared IR helpers into these aggregation files;
# each helper is exercised by the code that calls it (irgen generation, the ir
# optimizer/verifier) and by the moved integration tests in irgen — not by a
# dedicated per-file unit test.
pkg/binate/ir/ir_util_shared.bn
pkg/binate/ir/module_init_emit.bn
pkg/binate/ir/ir_iface_query.bn
# irutil is a leaf package of pure, individually-trivial helpers (string/type
# predicates, name manglers); covered via their many callers in ir/irgen and the
# conformance suite.
pkg/binate/irutil/util.bn
pkg/binate/irutil/nameutil.bn
#
# emit_sysv_thunk.bn — the x86-64 SysV #[c_export] entry-thunk parameter
# marshalling helpers (sysvWriteThunk*), split from emit_sysv_coerce.bn for
# length; all six are exercised (clang-verified IR) by emit_cexport_thunk_test.bn
# (TestEmitCExportThunk{SseAggParam,MixedSseStraddle,CMemInternalSse,CMemInternalGp}X64)
# and end-to-end by e2e/ffi-export.sh.
pkg/binate/codegen/emit_sysv_thunk.bn

# irdata/funcsig_index.bn holds the FuncSig hashing policy methods + funcSigHash,
# relocated with the FuncSig/ImplInfo/TypeInfoEntry satellite types; exercised via
# the module funcsig-index code and conformance.
pkg/binate/irdata/funcsig_index.bn

# vmdata/name_hash.bn — the VM name-index hash/eq policy methods + hashName/nameEq,
# relocated with the vmdata runtime types; exercised via the VM func-index code.
pkg/binate/vmdata/name_hash.bn

# aarch64_call_return.bn holds the caller-side return-value COLLECTION helpers
# (collectMultiReturnFields / storeMultiReturnTupleFieldsAA64 / collectScalarReturn /
# canonicalizeSubWordReturn), extracted from aarch64_call.bn purely for file length.
# They have no standalone surface — they run only as the tail of a call lowering — and are
# exercised by aarch64_call_test.bn's return-collection tests (aggregate-return spill, sret,
# void __c_call skip) plus the multi-return / aggregate-return conformance suite across native.
pkg/binate/native/aarch64/aarch64_call_return.bn

# struct_leaf.bn holds ManagedStructLeafEligible (+ its recursive helper
# isLeafManagedField), split out of the SROA pass so the leaf-eligibility predicate
# stays in the ir data model (irgen and the SROA candidate gate both consume it).
# Exercised cross-package by iropt/sroa_managed_test.bn's leaf-eligibility cases.
pkg/binate/ir/struct_leaf.bn

# inline_eligibility.bn holds the inliner's private eligibility analysis (no exported
# surface); it runs only as part of the inline pass and is exercised by
# iropt/inline_calls_test.bn / inline_recursion_test.bn.
pkg/binate/iropt/inline_eligibility.bn

# --- irbuild split (emit API extracted from ir) ---
# The emit builder files hold IR-construction free functions; their tests are the
# emit tests that moved with them (ir_test.bn, ir_ops_test.bn, ir_ops_flow/iface/
# managed_test.bn, ir_block_builder_test.bn), which build IR via the emit API and
# assert on the resulting instructions. Filenames don't line up 1:1 (the emit code
# was re-split into emit_core/emit_ops/emit_refdec/emit_satregistry), so the
# same-name check can't see the coverage.
pkg/binate/irbuild/emit_core.bn
pkg/binate/irbuild/emit_ops.bn
pkg/binate/irbuild/emit_refdec.bn
pkg/binate/irbuild/emit_satregistry.bn
pkg/binate/irbuild/module_init_emit.bn
# ir data-model/query files whose emit-using tests moved to irbuild (a package-`ir`
# test cannot import irbuild — cycle). Their staying surface (constructors,
# PeelToUnderlying/IsTerminator, CollectStrings/FinalizeStrings, CEntryTargetFunc)
# is exercised cross-package by irbuild's ir_test.bn / ir_ops_test.bn / strings_test.bn
# / data_satregistry_test.bn, which build IR via the emit API.
pkg/binate/ir/ir.bn
pkg/binate/ir/ir_ops.bn
pkg/binate/ir/strings.bn
pkg/binate/ir/data_satregistry.bn

# bytecode_ops.bn is the VM bytecode opcode enum (pure `const` declarations, no
# logic) — package-private, extracted from vm.bni (no external consumer). Nothing
# to unit-test; the opcodes are exercised end-to-end by the VM exec + lowering tests.
pkg/binate/vm/bytecode_ops.bn

# --- checker split (types -> types + check) ---
# These type data-model files' tests build fixtures via the type checker (which
# lives in pkg/binate/check now), so a package-`types` test can't import them
# (cycle). The tests moved to check/ (types_test.bn, types_const_test.bn,
# string_lit_test.bn, literal_value_test.bn, types_method_test.bn,
# types_identical_test.bn, types_query_test.bn) and exercise these files' surface
# cross-package.
pkg/binate/types/types.bn
pkg/binate/types/types_query.bn
pkg/binate/types/types_const.bn
pkg/binate/types/string_lit.bn
pkg/binate/types/literal_value.bn
pkg/binate/types/types_method.bn
pkg/binate/types/types_identical.bn
# char_util.bn is pure char/UTF-8/slice utilities (charEq/hexDigitVal/Utf8*) shared
# by the type model and the checker; exercised end-to-end by the checker + string
# tests, no standalone surface.
pkg/binate/types/char_util.bn
# type_helpers.bn holds the checker-only type-operation helpers extracted from the
# type-op files (comparability/const-checking/literal-parsing/type constructors);
# exercised by check's type-op tests (types_test.bn, types_const_test.bn, etc.).
pkg/binate/check/type_helpers.bn
